nscious effort, Shadbala Strong"]}, {"label": "Raja Yoga", "confidence": "mixed", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "Formed when the angular lord (Sun) and the trine lord (Mercury) join in one house — a Raja-yoga pattern supporting rise in status, provided the planets involved are reasonably strong. Strength is mixed — some support, some friction.", "factors": ["Mercury: in a neutral spot, Shadbala Strong, combust", "Sun: at its very best and very strong, Shadbala Strong"]}, {"label": "Harihara Brahma Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "Formed by any of three classical combinations linking the 2nd, 7th or Lagna lord with specific benefic placements — a Harihara Brahma yoga for eminent scholarship, truthfulness and a helpful nature.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Damni Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "All seven planets spread across exactly 6 distinct sign(s) (a Sankhya Nabhasa yoga) — classically: Highly charitable, always helping others, protector of cattle.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Duryoga", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "The 10th lord sits in a dusthana (6th, 8th or 12th) — a Duryoga where one's own efforts don't bring due credit, tempting shortcuts or deception.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Dehasthoulya Yoga (III)", "confidence": "mixed", "polarity": "mixed", "text": "The ascendant falls in a watery sign with benefics, or the lagna lord is itself a watery planet — a Dehasthoulya yoga for a stout physique.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Swaveeryaddhana Yoga (II)", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The dispositor of the lagna lord's Navamsa lord is strong and angular from the 2nd lord, or dignified — a Swaveeryaddhana yoga for self-earned wealth.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Swaveeryaddhana Yoga (III)", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The 2nd lord holds an angle or trine from the lagna lord, or a benefic 2nd lord is deeply exalted or joined by an exalted planet — a Swaveeryaddhana yoga for self-earned wealth.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Matrumooladdhana Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The 2nd lord joins or is aspected by the 4th lord — money earned with a mother's help.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Daridra Yoga (149)", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "The lagna lord is associated with a 6th/8th/12th lord and subjected to malefic aspects — dire poverty and want.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Asatyavadi Yoga", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "The 2nd lord sits in a sign of Saturn or Mars while malefics occupy an angle and a trine — the native tends toward untruthfulness.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Sumukha Yoga (II)", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "Benefics join the 2nd house — an attractive, smiling face.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Bhratruvriddhi Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The 3rd lord, Mars, or the 3rd house is joined or aspected by benefics — happiness through prosperous brothers.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Bandhubhisthyaktha Yoga", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "The 4th lord is associated with malefics or sits in an inimical/debilitated sign — deserted by relatives.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Matrunasa Yoga (I)", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "The Moon is hemmed in between, joined by, or aspected by malefics — a very early death of the mother.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Matru Satrutwa Yoga", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "The lagna and 4th lords are natural or temporal enemies — ill feeling between mother and son.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Vahana Yoga (I)", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The lagna lord joins the 4th, 9th, or 11th house — material comforts and conveyances.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Vahana Yoga (II)", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The 4th lord is exalted while its exaltation sign's lord holds an angle or trine — material comforts and conveyances.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Bahuputra Yoga (II)", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The Navamsa lord of a planet linked to the 7th lord sits in the 1st, 2nd or 5th — a large number of children.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Aputra Yoga", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "The 5th lord sits in a dusthana — no issues at all.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Satkalatra Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The 7th lord or Venus links to Jupiter or Mercury — a noble, chaste and virtuous spouse.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Raja Yoga (II)", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "A debilitated planet, uncombust or retrograde, still holds an angle or trine — rank equal to a ruler.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Neechabhanga Raja Yoga (III)", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "A debilitated planet's dispositor or exaltation-lord holds an angle from the Moon or Lagna — cancelling the debilitation and ushering in royal luck from humble beginnings.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Raja Yoga (XI)", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The Navamsa lord of the Moon's sign holds an angle or trine from the Lagna or Mercury — a highly respectable position.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Guhyaroga Yoga", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "The Moon joins malefics in the Navamsa of Cancer or Scorpio — diseases of the private parts, piles or hernia.", "factors": []}]}
