his coming chapter brings growth, wisdom, teaching, finances, children and good counsel to the fore."}, {"label": "Saturn life period · age 83–102 (ahead)", "confidence": "moderate", "text": "13 Dec 2076 → 13 Dec 2095 (19 yrs): This coming chapter brings discipline, hard work, responsibility, structure and patience to the fore."}]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 13, "total": 25, "id": "dasha_timeline", "title_en": "Life-period timeline (with dates)", "title_ne": "जीवन-कालखण्ड तालिका", "body": ["The schedule of sub-periods inside your current Moon life period, and the big life periods that follow — the most precise timing layer of your chart."], "items": [{"label": "Mars sub-period · running now", "confidence": "mixed", "text": "14 Oct 2026 → 15 May 2027: drive — linked to your 10th house."}, {"label": "Rahu sub-period", "confidence": "tentative", "text": "15 May 2027 → 13 Nov 2028: ambition — linked to your 12th house."}, {"label": "Mars life period (next major chapter)", "confidence": "moderate", "text": "Begins 14 Dec 2035, lasting to 14 Dec 2042 (7 yrs): a drive chapter."}, {"label": "Rahu life period (next major chapter)", "confidence": "moderate", "text": "Begins 14 Dec 2042, lasting to 13 Dec 2060 (18 yrs): a ambition chapter."}, {"label": "Jupiter life period (next major chapter)", "confidence": "moderate", "text": "Begins 13 Dec 2060, lasting to 13 Dec 2076 (16 yrs): a growth chapter."}]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 14, "total": 25, "id": "outlook_12_months", "title_en": "Outlook — next 12 months", "title_ne": "आगामी १२ महिना", "body": ["The year ahead is led by Mars's sub-period (through 15 May 2027), bringing drive, property, technical or competitive effort and bold initiative to the fore.", "It is well placed (in your 10th house), so initiatives in its areas are favoured — a good window to push forward.", "A shift to come: the Rahu sub-period opens 15 May 2027, bringing ambition to the foreground."], "confidence": "tentative", "factors": ["Dasha: Moon runs the current mahadasha"]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 15, "total": 25, "id": "pursue_and_when", "title_en": "What to pursue & when", "title_ne": "के कुरामा लाग्ने र कहिले", "body": ["This section shows what to focus on and the best time for each one. Every life area below comes with the period that most favours it — try to line up your bigger decisions with those good times."], "items": [{"label": "Your strongest area", "confidence": "moderate", "text": "You are naturally good at discipline, patience and steady hard work — effort pays off fastest here, so put most of your energy into it. Best time for this: an upcoming good period (15 Mar 2030 → 14 Oct 2031)."}, {"label": "Career & work", "confidence": "moderate", "text": "Make your bigger moves in career, status and public role. Best time for this: an upcoming good period (14 Oct 2031 → 14 Mar 2033)."}, {"label": "Wealth & gains", "confidence": "mixed", "text": "Expand income streams, networks and aspirations. Best time for this: an upcoming good period (14 Oct 2033 → 14 Jun 2035)."}, {"label": "Relationships & partnership", "confidence": "moderate", "text": "Advance marriage, partnership or public collaboration. Best time for this: an upcoming good period (14 Oct 2031 → 14 Mar 2033)."}, {"label": "Learning, dharma & mentors", "confidence": "moderate", "text": "Invest in higher learning, travel, mentors and spiritual practice. Best time for this: an upcoming good period (14 Jun 2035 → 14 Dec 2035)."}]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 16, "total": 25, "id": "opportunities", "title_en": "Opportunities", "title_ne": "अवसर", "body": ["The 1st house (self) is well supported — a natural area to invest energy.", "The 5th house (intelligence) is well supported — a natural area to invest energy.", "The 9th house (fortune) is well supported — a natural area to invest energy.", "Gaja-Kesari Yoga: Formed when Jupiter sits in an angle (kendra) from the Moon — a classic combination for good judgement, respect and steady fortune that tends to ripen with maturity.", "Sunapha Yoga: Planets (other than the Sun) occupy the 2nd house from the Moon — a Chandra yoga for self-made prosperity and reputation built through personal effort.", "Anapha Yoga: Planets occupy the 12th house from the Moon — a Chandra yoga for refinement, comfort and graceful conduct that attracts support from others.", "Durdhara Yoga: Planets flank the Moon on both the 2nd and 12th sides — a strong Chandra yoga for wealth, vehicles and a life supported by resources on every side.", "Amala Yoga: A natural benefic occupies the 10th house from the Lagna or the Moon — a spotless (amala) reputation yoga for ethical conduct and lasting public respect.", "Veshi Yoga: Planets occupy the 2nd house from the Sun — a Surya yoga for truthful speech, integrity and recognition through principled action.", "Vasi Yoga: Planets occupy the 12th house from the Sun — a Surya yoga for charity, spiritual merit and influence through selfless service.", "Ubhayachari Yoga: Planets flank the Sun on both the 2nd and 12th sides — a balanced Surya yoga for all-round ability, balanced temperament and success in both worldly and dharmic pursuits.", "Budha-Aditya Yoga: Formed when the Sun and Mercury share a sign, favouring intelligence, clear expression and analytical or administrative ability (strongest when Mercury is not too close/combust).", "Mahabhagya Yoga: The lagna, Sun and Moon all fall in signs of the same parity, matching day/night birth (all odd signs by day, all even by night) — a great-fortune yoga for overall luck, health and supportive circumstances through life.", "Parijata Yoga: The dispositor of the lagna lord's sign, or the Navamsa lord of that dispositor, falls in a kendra, trikona, or own/exaltation sign — a Parijata yoga for happiness in mid and later life, honoured by leaders.", "Raja Yoga: Formed when the angular lord (Jupiter) and the trine lord (Mars) join in one house — a Raja-yoga pattern supporting rise in status, provided the planets involved are reasonably strong.", "Raja Yoga: Formed when the angular lord (Mercury) and the trine lord (Sun) join in one house — a Raja-yoga pattern supporting rise in status, provided the planets involved are reasonably strong.", "Harihara Brahma Yoga: Formed by any of three classical combinations linking the 2nd, 7th or Lagna lord with specific benefic placements — a Harihara Brahma yoga for eminent scholarship, truthfulness and a helpful nature.", "Ardha Chandra Yoga: All seven planets occupy seven contiguous houses beginning from a Panapara or Apoklima house — an Ardha Chandra yoga for fine features, lifelong happiness and command.", "Pasa Yoga: All seven planets spread across exactly 5 distinct sign(s) (a Sankhya Nabhasa yoga) — classically: Acquires wealth righteously, surrounded by friends and relatives.", "Sareera Soukhya Yoga: The lagna lord, Jupiter or Venus occupies an angle — a Sareera Soukhya yoga for long life, wealth and political favour.", "Swaveeryaddhana Yoga (III): The 2nd lord holds an angle or trine from the lagna lord, or a benefic 2nd lord is deeply exalted or joined by an exalted planet — a Swaveeryaddhana yoga for self-earned wealth.", "Madhya Vayasi Dhana Yoga: The 2nd lord stands in an angle/trine from both the lagna and 11th lords, aspected by a benefic — money earned by one's own effort in the middle years.", "Bhratruvriddhi Yoga: The 3rd lord, Mars, or the 3rd house is joined or aspected by benefics — happiness through prosperous brothers.", "Uttama Griha Yoga: The 4th lord joins benefics in a kendra or trikona — good houses.", "Bandhu Pujya Yoga (II): The 4th house or its lord has the association or aspect of Jupiter — respected and loved by relatives and friends.", "Nishkapata Yoga (I): The 4th house is occupied by a benefic, a dignified planet, or is itself a benefic sign — a Nishkapata yoga for a pure heart that hates secrecy and hypocrisy.", "Matru Sneha Yoga: The lagna and 4th lords share lordship, are natural or temporal friends, or the 4th is aspected by a benefic — cordial relations between mother and son.", "Ekaputra Yoga: The 5th lord joins an angle or trine — only one son.", "Satkalatra Yoga: The 7th lord or Venus links to Jupiter or Mercury — a noble, chaste and virtuous spouse.", "Raja Yoga (III): Two to four planets possess Digbala (directional strength) — a ruler even from an ordinary family.", "Raja Yoga (IX): The 10th lord in the 9th holds a dignified Navamsa — a ruler or an equal.", "Raja Yoga (XI): The Navamsa lord of the Moon's sign holds an angle or trine from the Lagna or Mercury — a highly respectable position."]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 17, "total": 25, "id": "cautions", "title_en": "Areas for caution", "title_ne": "सावधानी", "body": ["Keep a steady hand with release (the 12th house) — manage rather than force.", "Keep a steady hand with work (the 6th house) — manage rather than force.", "Vanchana Chora Bheeti Yoga: The Lagna holds a malefic with Gulika in a trine, or Gulika joins a kendra/trikona lord, or the lagna lord conjoins Rahu, Saturn or Ketu — a caution yoga classically linked to suspicion, fear of being cheated, swindled or robbed; clear boundaries and verifying people/deals directly help.", "Daridra Yoga: The 11th lord sits in a dusthana (6th, 8th or 12th) — a Daridra yoga for financial strain, debt and a mean disposition unless corrected by other strong factors.", "Dehakashta Yoga: The lagna lord joins a malefic or sits in the 8th house — a Dehakashta yoga pointing to reduced bodily comfort.", "Rogagrastha Yoga: The lagna lord in the ascendant joins a 6th/8th/12th lord, or a weak lagna lord sits in an angle or trine — a Rogagrastha yoga for a delicate constitution prone to sickness.", "Daridra Yoga (149): The lagna lord is associated with a 6th/8th/12th lord and subjected to malefic aspects — dire poverty and want.", "Asatyavadi Yoga: The 2nd lord sits in a sign of Saturn or Mars while malefics occupy an angle and a trine — the native tends toward untruthfulness.", "Durmukha Yoga (I): Malefics occupy the 2nd while its lord joins an evil planet or is debilitated — an unattractive face and an irritable temper.", "Sraddhannabhuktha Yoga: Saturn owns or joins the 2nd lord, or the 2nd is aspected by a debilitated Saturn — food from death ceremonies.", "Vishaprayoga Yoga: The 2nd house is joined and aspected by malefics while its lord sits in a cruel Navamsa aspected by a malefic — poisoned by others.", "Bandhubhisthyaktha Yoga: The 4th lord is associated with malefics or sits in an inimical/debilitated sign — deserted by relatives.", "Matrunasa Yoga (I): The Moon is hemmed in between, joined by, or aspected by malefics — a very early death of the mother.", "None of these are predictions of misfortune — they are areas where awareness and moderation protect your progress."]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 18, "total": 25, "id": "practical_recommendations", "title_en": "Practical recommendations", "title_ne": "व्यावहारिक सुझाव", "body": ["Play to your strengths — discipline, patience and steady hard work. This is where progress comes easiest for you.", "Don't avoid your weaker side — clear thinking, communication and learning. Build it up slowly with small, regular habits instead of waiting until you feel ready.", "Save big decisions for the good times highlighted above, so you act when the timing is on your side.", "Pick one small habit for each priority below and stick with it for the next three months."]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 19, "total": 25, "id": "spiritual_practices", "title_en": "Traditional spiritual practices (optional)", "title_ne": "पारम्परिक उपाय (वैकल्पिक)", "body": ["These are traditional, faith-based remedies offered as optional support — they are cultural practices, not requirements or guarantees.", "For strengthening Mercury themes, classical texts suggest its weekday observance, charity associated with Mercury, and respectful, calm conduct in that life area.", "Gratitude practices around Saturn themes help you make the most of an existing strength.", "Above all, ethical action (sadachara) and steadiness are the remedies every tradition agrees on."], "optional": true}
{"kind": "section", "index": 20, "total": 25, "id": "planet_by_planet", "title_en": "Planet by planet", "title_ne": "ग्रह विश्लेषण", "body": [], "items": [{"label": "Sun (सूर्य)", "confidence": "moderate", "factors": ["D1: Sun very comfortable and strong", "Shadbala: Strong"], "text": "Sun is in Simha at 8°49′ (birth star Magha, quarter 3), in your 9th house; and is very comfortable and strong there. In life it stands for soul, vitality, father, authority and self-confidence. Its overall strength is strong."}, {"label": "Moon (चन्द्र)", "confidence": "tentative", "factors": ["Dasha: Moon runs the current mahadasha"], "text": "Moon is in Dhanu at 1°20′ (birth star Mula, quarter 1), in your 1st house; and is in a neutral spot there. In life it stands for mind, emotions, mother, comfort and the public. Its overall strength is adequate."}, {"label": "Mars (मंगल)", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["Shadbala: Strong", "Dasha: Mars runs the current antardasha", "D1: Mars in an enemy sign"], "text": "Mars is in Kanya at 14°43′ (birth star Hasta, quarter 2), in your 10th house; and is a little strained there. In life it stands for energy, courage, drive, siblings and property. Its overall strength is strong."}, {"label": "Mercury (बुध)", "confidence": "moderate", "factors": ["D1: Mercury in a friendly sign", "D9: Mercury dignified in navamsa"], "text": "Mercury is in Simha at 6°50′ (birth star Magha, quarter 3), in your 9th house; and is well supported there; very close to the Sun (combust), so its outer results take extra effort. In life it stands for intellect, communication, commerce and learning. Its overall strength is adequate."}, {"label": "Jupiter (बृहस्पति)", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["Shadbala: Strong", "D1: Jupiter in an enemy sign"], "text": "Jupiter is in Kanya at 23°56′ (birth star Chitra, quarter 1), in your 10th house; and is a little strained there. In life it stands for wisdom, ethics, wealth, teachers, children and grace. Its overall strength is strong."}, {"label": "Venus (शुक्र)", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["Shadbala: Strong", "D1: Venus in an enemy sign", "D9: Venus weak in navamsa"], "text": "Venus is in Karka at 7°43′ (birth star Pushya, quarter 2), in your 8th house; and is a little strained there. In life it stands for love, partnership, beauty, comfort and the arts. Its overall strength is strong."}, {"label": "Saturn (शनि)", "confidence": "moderate", "factors": ["D1: Saturn steady and self-assured", "Shadbala: Strong"], "text": "Saturn is in Makara at 23°59′ (birth star Dhanishta, quarter 1), in your 2nd house; and is steady and self-assured there; moving backwards for now (retrograde), so its themes turn inward and get revisited. In life it stands for discipline, endurance, work, service and longevity. Its overall strength is strong."}, {"label": "Rahu (राहु)", "confidence": "tentative", "factors": [], "text": "Rahu is in Vrishchika at 17°57′ (birth star Jyeshtha, quarter 1), in your 12th house. In life it stands for ambition, foreign and unconventional paths, obsession."}, {"label": "Ketu (केतु)", "confidence": "tentative", "factors": [], "text": "Ketu is in Vrishabha at 17°57′ (birth star Rohini, quarter 3), in your 6th house. In life it stands for detachment, intuition, past mastery and liberation."}]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 21, "total": 25, "id": "house_by_house", "title_en": "House by house", "title_ne": "भाव विश्लेषण", "body": [], "items": [{"label": "Self (house 1)", "confidence": "strong", "factors": ["D1: 1st lord in a strong angle/trine (the 10th)", "Shadbala: 1st lord Strong", "D1: natural benefic(s) present — Moon"], "text": "This area of life is about self, body, vitality and overall life direction. The planet in charge of it, Jupiter, currently sits in the part of your chart about career, and is a little strained there (overall strength strong). Planets currently in this area: Moon."}, {"label": "Wealth (house 2)", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["D1: 2nd lord Saturn well dignified", "Shadbala: 2nd lord Strong", "D1: natural malefic(s) present — Saturn"], "text": "This area of life is about wealth, speech, family lineage and nourishment. The planet in charge of it, Saturn, currently sits in the part of your chart about wealth, and is steady and self-assured there (overall strength strong). Planets currently in this area: Saturn."}, {"label": "Courage (house 3)", "confidence": "moderate", "factors": ["D1: 3rd lord Saturn well dignified", "Shadbala: 3rd lord Strong"], "text": "This area of life is about courage, effort, siblings, communication and skill. The planet in charge of it, Saturn, currently sits in the part of your chart about wealth, and is steady and self-assured there (overall strength strong)."}, {"label": "Home (house 4)", "confidence": "moderate", "factors": ["D1: 4th lord in a strong angle/trine (the 10th)", "Shadbala: 4th lord Strong"], "text": "This area of life is about home, mother, inner peace, property and education. The planet in charge of it, Jupiter, currently sits in the part of your chart about career, and is a little strained there (overall strength strong)."}, {"label": "Intelligence (house 5)", "confidence": "moderate", "factors": ["D1: 5th lord in a strong angle/trine (the 10th)", "Shadbala: 5th lord Strong"], "text": "This area of life is about intelligence, creativity, children and past merit. The planet in charge of it, Mars, currently sits in the part of your chart about career, and is a little strained there (overall strength strong)."}, {"label": "Work (house 6)", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["Shadbala: 6th lord Strong", "D1: malefic(s) in an upachaya house (strengthening here) — Ketu", "D1: 6th lord falls in the 8th (a difficult house)"], "text": "This area of life is about work, service, health, competition and obstacles. The planet in charge of it, Venus, currently sits in the part of your chart about transformation, and is a little strained there (overall strength strong). Planets currently in this area: Ketu."}, {"label": "Partnership (house 7)", "confidence": "tentative", "factors": ["D1: 7th lord in a strong angle/trine (the 9th)"], "text": "This area of life is about partnership, marriage, business and public dealings. The planet in charge of it, Mercury, currently sits in the part of your chart about fortune, and is well supported there (overall strength adequate)."}, {"label": "Transformation (house 8)", "confidence": "moderate", "factors": ["D1: 8th lord in a strong angle/trine (the 1st)", "D1: natural benefic(s) present — Venus"], "text": "This area of life is about transformation, shared resources, research and longevity. The planet in charge of it, Moon, currently sits in the part of your chart about self, and is in a neutral spot there (overall strength adequate). Planets currently in this area: Venus."}, {"label": "Fortune (house 9)", "confidence": "strong", "factors": ["D1: 9th lord Sun well dignified", "D1: 9th lord in a strong angle/trine (the 9th)", "Shadbala: 9th lord Strong", "D1: natural benefic(s) present — Mercury", "D1: natural malefic(s) present — Sun"], "text": "This area of life is about fortune, dharma, higher learning, mentors and the father. The planet in charge of it, Sun, currently sits in the part of your chart about fortune, and is very comfortable and strong there (overall strength strong). Planets currently in this area: Sun, Mercury."}, {"label": "Career (house 10)", "confidence": "strong", "factors": ["D1: 10th lord in a strong angle/trine (the 9th)", "D1: natural benefic(s) present — Jupiter", "D1: malefic(s) in an upachaya house (strengthening here) — Mars"], "text": "This area of life is about career, status, public role and worldly action. The planet in charge of it, Mercury, currently sits in the part of your chart about fortune, and is well supported there (overall strength adequate). Planets currently in this area: Mars, Jupiter."}, {"label": "Gains (house 11)", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["Shadbala: 11th lord Strong", "D1: 11th lord falls in the 8th (a difficult house)"], "text": "This area of life is about gains, networks, aspirations and elder siblings. The planet in charge of it, Venus, currently sits in the part of your chart about transformation, and is a little strained there (overall strength strong)."}, {"label": "Release (house 12)", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["D1: 12th lord in a strong angle/trine (the 10th)", "Shadbala: 12th lord Strong", "D1: natural malefic(s) present — Rahu"], "text": "This area of life is about release, expenses, retreat, foreign lands and liberation. The planet in charge of it, Mars, currently sits in the part of your chart about career, and is a little strained there (overall strength strong). Planets currently in this area: Rahu."}]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 22, "total": 25, "id": "divisional_charts", "title_en": "Divisional charts (D-charts) summary", "title_ne": "वर्ग चक्र (D-चार्ट) सारांश", "body": ["Divisional (varga) charts subdivide each rashi of the birth chart into finer parts, and each one zooms in on a specific area of life. Below is a short reading of what every major D-chart is read for and how strong that area looks in this chart."], "items": [{"label": "D9 — Navamsa", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["Mercury: steady and self-assured", "Venus: weak and needing conscious effort"], "text": "The D9 chart (Navamsa) shows your marriage, dharma, fortune and the inner strength of every planet. Mercury is strong here, which helps this area. Venus is under some strain, so this part needs more care. Overall, this area looks mixed — some support and some challenges."}, {"label": "D10 — Dasamsa", "confidence": "moderate", "factors": ["Sun: weak and needing conscious effort", "Moon: keeps its natal sign", "Mars: keeps its natal sign", "Jupiter: steady and self-assured", "Venus: steady and self-assured", "Saturn: weak and needing conscious effort"], "text": "The D10 chart (Dasamsa) shows your career, profession, status and public achievement. Jupiter, Venus, Moon, Mars are strong here, which helps this area. Sun, Saturn are under some strain, so this part needs more care. Overall, this area looks reasonably supported."}, {"label": "D7 — Saptamsa", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["Sun: weak and needing conscious effort", "Moon: keeps its natal sign", "Mercury: at its very best and very strong"], "text": "The D7 chart (Saptamsa) shows your children, progeny and creative continuity. Mercury, Moon are strong here, which helps this area. Sun is under some strain, so this part needs more care. Overall, this area looks mixed — some support and some challenges."}, {"label": "D4 — Chaturthamsa", "confidence": "strong", "factors": ["Moon: keeps its natal sign", "Mercury: keeps its natal sign", "Venus: steady and self-assured", "Saturn: at its very best and very strong"], "text": "The D4 chart (Chaturthamsa) shows your home, land, property and inner contentment. Venus, Saturn, Moon, Mercury are strong here, which helps this area. Overall, this area looks strong and well-supported."}, {"label": "D12 — Dwadashamsa", "confidence": "strong", "factors": ["Moon: keeps its natal sign", "Venus: steady and self-assured", "Saturn: at its very best and very strong"], "text": "The D12 chart (Dwadashamsa) shows your parents, lineage and inherited karma. Venus, Saturn, Moon are strong here, which helps this area. Overall, this area looks strong and well-supported."}, {"label": "D24 — Chaturvimsamsa", "confidence": "moderate", "factors": ["Saturn: very comfortable and strong"], "text": "The D24 chart (Chaturvimsamsa) shows your education, learning and scholarship. Saturn is strong here, which helps this area. Overall, this area looks reasonably supported."}, {"label": "D2 — Hora", "confidence": "moderate", "factors": ["Sun: very comfortable and strong, keeps its natal sign", "Mars: weak and needing conscious effort", "Mercury: keeps its natal sign", "Venus: keeps its natal sign"], "text": "The D2 chart (Hora) shows your wealth, resources and material sustenance. Sun, Mercury, Venus are strong here, which helps this area. Mars is under some strain, so this part needs more care. Overall, this area looks reasonably supported."}, {"label": "D3 — Drekkana", "confidence": "strong", "factors": ["Sun: very comfortable and strong, keeps its natal sign", "Moon: keeps its natal sign", "Mars: at its very best and very strong", "Mercury: keeps its natal sign", "Venus: keeps its natal sign"], "text": "The D3 chart (Drekkana) shows your siblings, courage and personal initiative. Sun, Mars, Moon, Mercury, Venus are strong here, which helps this area. Overall, this area looks strong and well-supported."}, {"label": "D16 — Shodashamsa", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["Moon: keeps its natal sign", "Mars: weak and needing conscious effort", "Jupiter: steady and self-assured", "Saturn: weak and needing conscious effort"], "text": "The D16 chart (Shodashamsa) shows your vehicles, comforts and material pleasures. Jupiter, Moon are strong here, which helps this area. Mars, Saturn are under some strain, so this part needs more care. Overall, this area looks mixed — some support and some challenges."}, {"label": "D20 — Vimsamsa", "confidence": "tentative", "factors": ["Venus: weak and needing conscious effort"], "text": "The D20 chart (Vimsamsa) shows your spiritual practice, devotion and religious merit. Venus is under some strain, so this part needs more care. Overall, this area looks average, without a standout signal."}, {"label": "D27 — Bhamsa", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["Moon: at its very best and very strong", "Venus: keeps its natal sign", "Saturn: weak and needing conscious effort"], "text": "The D27 chart (Bhamsa) shows your innate strengths, weaknesses and stamina. Moon, Venus are strong here, which helps this area. Saturn is under some strain, so this part needs more care. Overall, this area looks mixed — some support and some challenges."}, {"label": "D30 — Trimsamsa", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["Jupiter: weak and needing conscious effort", "Venus: weak and needing conscious effort", "Saturn: steady and self-assured, keeps its natal sign"], "text": "The D30 chart (Trimsamsa) shows your adversity, health risks and moral fibre. Saturn is strong here, which helps this area. Jupiter, Venus are under some strain, so this part needs more care. Overall, this area looks mixed — some support and some challenges."}, {"label": "D60 — Shashtiamsa", "confidence": "moderate", "factors": ["Mercury: at its very best and very strong", "Venus: steady and self-assured"], "text": "The D60 chart (Shashtiamsa) shows your the sum of past-life karma standing behind the whole chart. Mercury, Venus are strong here, which helps this area. Overall, this area looks reasonably supported."}]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 23, "total": 25, "id": "yoga_explanations", "title_en": "Yogas in your chart", "title_ne": "योग", "body": ["A yoga is a specific planetary combination that inclines the chart toward a particular tendency. Below are the yogas formed in your chart, with the strength of the planets involved and whether the running dasha is activating them."], "items": [{"label": "Gaja-Kesari Yoga", "confidence": "strong", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "Formed when Jupiter sits in an angle (kendra) from the Moon — a classic combination for good judgement, respect and steady fortune that tends to ripen with maturity. Its planets are strong here, so the result is dependable; the running dasha is activating it now.", "factors": ["Jupiter: a little strained, Shadbala Strong", "Moon: in a neutral spot, Shadbala Adequate", "Activated by the current dasha"]}, {"label": "Sunapha Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "Planets (other than the Sun) occupy the 2nd house from the Moon — a Chandra yoga for self-made prosperity and reputation built through personal effort.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Anapha Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "Planets occupy the 12th house from the Moon — a Chandra yoga for refinement, comfort and graceful conduct that attracts support from others.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Durdhara Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "Planets flank the Moon on both the 2nd and 12th sides — a strong Chandra yoga for wealth, vehicles and a life supported by resources on every side.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Vanchana Chora Bheeti Yoga", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "The Lagna holds a malefic with Gulika in a trine, or Gulika joins a kendra/trikona lord, or the lagna lord conjoins Rahu, Saturn or Ketu — a caution yoga classically linked to suspicion, fear of being cheated, swindled or robbed; clear boundaries and verifying people/deals directly help.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Amala Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "A natural benefic occupies the 10th house from the Lagna or the Moon — a spotless (amala) reputation yoga for ethical conduct and lasting public respect.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Veshi Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "Planets occupy the 2nd house from the Sun — a Surya yoga for truthful speech, integrity and recognition through principled action.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Vasi Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "Planets occupy the 12th house from the Sun — a Surya yoga for charity, spiritual merit and influence through selfless service.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Ubhayachari Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "Planets flank the Sun on both the 2nd and 12th sides — a balanced Surya yoga for all-round ability, balanced temperament and success in both worldly and dharmic pursuits.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Budha-Aditya Yoga", "confidence": "mixed", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "Formed when the Sun and Mercury share a sign, favouring intelligence, clear expression and analytical or administrative ability (strongest when Mercury is not too close/combust). Strength is mixed — some support, some friction.", "factors": ["Sun: very comfortable and strong, Shadbala Strong", "Mercury: well supported, Shadbala Adequate, combust"]}, {"label": "Mahabhagya Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The lagna, Sun and Moon all fall in signs of the same parity, matching day/night birth (all odd signs by day, all even by night) — a great-fortune yoga for overall luck, health and supportive circumstances through life.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Parijata Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The dispositor of the lagna lord's sign, or the Navamsa lord of that dispositor, falls in a kendra, trikona, or own/exaltation sign — a P