 a sign of Saturn or Mars while malefics occupy an angle and a trine — the native tends toward untruthfulness.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Durmukha Yoga (I)", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "Malefics occupy the 2nd while its lord joins an evil planet or is debilitated — an unattractive face and an irritable temper.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Sraddhannabhuktha Yoga", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "Saturn owns or joins the 2nd lord, or the 2nd is aspected by a debilitated Saturn — food from death ceremonies.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Vishaprayoga Yoga", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "The 2nd house is joined and aspected by malefics while its lord sits in a cruel Navamsa aspected by a malefic — poisoned by others.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Bhratruvriddhi Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The 3rd lord, Mars, or the 3rd house is joined or aspected by benefics — happiness through prosperous brothers.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Uttama Griha Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The 4th lord joins benefics in a kendra or trikona — good houses.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Bandhu Pujya Yoga (II)", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The 4th house or its lord has the association or aspect of Jupiter — respected and loved by relatives and friends.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Bandhubhisthyaktha Yoga", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "The 4th lord is associated with malefics or sits in an inimical/debilitated sign — deserted by relatives.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Matrunasa Yoga (I)", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "The Moon is hemmed in between, joined by, or aspected by malefics — a very early death of the mother.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Nishkapata Yoga (I)", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The 4th house is occupied by a benefic, a dignified planet, or is itself a benefic sign — a Nishkapata yoga for a pure heart that hates secrecy and hypocrisy.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Matru Sneha Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The lagna and 4th lords share lordship, are natural or temporal friends, or the 4th is aspected by a benefic — cordial relations between mother and son.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Ekaputra Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The 5th lord joins an angle or trine — only one son.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Satkalatra Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The 7th lord or Venus links to Jupiter or Mercury — a noble, chaste and virtuous spouse.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Raja Yoga (III)", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "Two to four planets possess Digbala (directional strength) — a ruler even from an ordinary family.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Raja Yoga (IX)", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The 10th lord in the 9th holds a dignified Navamsa — a ruler or an equal.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Raja Yoga (XI)", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "The Navamsa lord of the Moon's sign holds an angle or trine from the Lagna or Mercury — a highly respectable position.", "factors": []}]}
