{"kind": "section", "index": 13, "total": 23, "id": "pursue_and_when", "title_en": "What to pursue & when", "title_ne": "के कुरामा लाग्ने र कहिले", "body": ["This section shows what to focus on and the best time for each one. Every life area below comes with the period that most favours it — try to line up your bigger decisions with those good times."], "items": [{"label": "Your strongest area", "confidence": "strong", "text": "You are naturally good at learning, good judgement and steady growth — effort pays off fastest here, so put most of your energy into it."}, {"label": "Career & work", "confidence": "moderate", "text": "Make your bigger moves in career, status and public role."}, {"label": "Wealth & gains", "confidence": "strong", "text": "Expand income streams, networks and aspirations."}, {"label": "Relationships & partnership", "confidence": "mixed", "text": "Advance marriage, partnership or public collaboration."}, {"label": "Learning, dharma & mentors", "confidence": "mixed", "text": "Invest in higher learning, travel, mentors and spiritual practice."}]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 14, "total": 23, "id": "opportunities", "title_en": "Opportunities", "title_ne": "अवसर", "body": ["The 11th house (gains) is well supported — a natural area to invest energy.", "Sunapha Yoga: Planets (other than the Sun) occupy the 2nd house from the Moon — a Chandra yoga for self-made prosperity and reputation built through personal effort.", "Amala Yoga: A natural benefic occupies the 10th house from the Lagna or the Moon — a spotless (amala) reputation yoga for ethical conduct and lasting public respect.", "Parvata Yoga: Benefics occupy angular houses while the 6th and 8th houses are empty or hold only benefics — a Parvata yoga for generosity, prosperity and a life that rises like a mountain despite obstacles.", "Veshi Yoga: Planets occupy the 2nd house from the Sun — a Surya yoga for truthful speech, integrity and recognition through principled action.", "Vasi Yoga: Planets occupy the 12th house from the Sun — a Surya yoga for charity, spiritual merit and influence through selfless service.", "Ubhayachari Yoga: Planets flank the Sun on both the 2nd and 12th sides — a balanced Surya yoga for all-round ability, balanced temperament and success in both worldly and dharmic pursuits.", "Budha-Aditya Yoga: Formed when the Sun and Mercury share a sign, favouring intelligence, clear expression and analytical or administrative ability (strongest when Mercury is not too close/combust).", "Mahabhagya Yoga: The lagna, Sun and Moon all fall in signs of the same parity, matching day/night birth (all odd signs by day, all even by night) — a great-fortune yoga for overall luck, health and supportive circumstances through life.", "Chapa (Nabhasa) Yoga: All seven planets occupy the seven houses counted from the 10th (the 10th through the 4th) — a Nabhasa 'bow' yoga classically linked to comfort in the earlier and later phases of life.", "Parijata Yoga: The dispositor of the lagna lord's sign, or the Navamsa lord of that dispositor, falls in a kendra, trikona, or own/exaltation sign — a Parijata yoga for happiness in mid and later life, honoured by leaders.", "Raja Yoga: Formed when the angular lord (Mars) and the trine lord (Mercury) join in one house — a Raja-yoga pattern supporting rise in status, provided the planets involved are reasonably strong.", "Raja Yoga: Formed when the angular lord (Mars) and the trine lord (Saturn) join in one house — a Raja-yoga pattern supporting rise in status, provided the planets involved are reasonably strong.", "Raja Yoga: Formed when the angular lord (Saturn) and the trine lord (Mercury) join in one house — a Raja-yoga pattern supporting rise in status, provided the planets involved are reasonably strong.", "Raja Yoga: Formed when the angular lord (Sun) and the trine lord (Mercury) join in one house — a Raja-yoga pattern supporting rise in status, provided the planets involved are reasonably strong.", "Raja Yoga: Formed when the angular lord (Sun) and the trine lord (Saturn) join in one house — a Raja-yoga pattern supporting rise in status, provided the planets involved are reasonably strong.", "Dhana Yoga: Formed when the lords of income (2nd) and gains (11th) combine in one house — a wealth-forming pattern that rewards consistent earning and saving habits.", "Thrilochana Yoga: The Sun, Moon and Mars stand in mutual trines — a Thrilochana yoga for great wealth, intelligence and a formidable presence.", "Ardha Chandra Yoga: All seven planets occupy seven contiguous houses beginning from a Panapara or Apoklima house — an Ardha Chandra yoga for fine features, lifelong happiness and command.", "Kedara Yoga: All seven planets spread across exactly 4 distinct sign(s) (a Sankhya Nabhasa yoga) — classically: Earns a livelihood by agriculture, helpful.", "Sareera Soukhya Yoga: The lagna lord, Jupiter or Venus occupies an angle — a Sareera Soukhya yoga for long life, wealth and political favour.", "Swaveeryaddhana Yoga (II): The dispositor of the lagna lord's Navamsa lord is strong and angular from the 2nd lord, or dignified — a Swaveeryaddhana yoga for self-earned wealth.", "Yukthi Samanwithavagmi Yoga (I): The 2nd lord joins a benefic in an angle or trine, or is deeply exalted with Jupiter — the person becomes an eloquent, skilled speaker.", "Bhratruvriddhi Yoga: The 3rd lord, Mars, or the 3rd house is joined or aspected by benefics — happiness through prosperous brothers.", "Parakrama Yoga: The 3rd lord in a benefic Navamsa, linked to benefics, with Mars in a benefic sign — much courage.", "Bandhu Pujya Yoga (II): The 4th house or its lord has the association or aspect of Jupiter — respected and loved by relatives and friends.", "Nishkapata Yoga (I): The 4th house is occupied by a benefic, a dignified planet, or is itself a benefic sign — a Nishkapata yoga for a pure heart that hates secrecy and hypocrisy.", "Matru Sneha Yoga: The lagna and 4th lords share lordship, are natural or temporal friends, or the 4th is aspected by a benefic — cordial relations between mother and son.", "Vahana Yoga (I): The lagna lord joins the 4th, 9th, or 11th house — material comforts and conveyances.", "Buddhimaturya Yoga: A benefic 5th lord is aspected by another benefic, or sits in a benefic sign — great intelligence and character.", "Satkalatra Yoga: The 7th lord or Venus links to Jupiter or Mercury — a noble, chaste and virtuous spouse.", "Raja Yoga (III): Two to four planets possess Digbala (directional strength) — a ruler even from an ordinary family.", "Raja Yoga (XI): The Navamsa lord of the Moon's sign holds an angle or trine from the Lagna or Mercury — a highly respectable position.", "Raja Yoga (XIV): One of the 11th/9th/2nd lords holds an angle from the Moon while Jupiter rules the 2nd, 5th or 11th — greatness and high leadership."]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 15, "total": 23, "id": "cautions", "title_en": "Areas for caution", "title_ne": "सावधानी", "body": ["Kala Sarpa Yoga: All seven tara grahas fall on one side of the Rahu–Ketu axis with none breaking out of the nodal hemisphere — a pattern associated with karmic intensity and sudden reversals in life direction.", "Vanchana Chora Bheeti Yoga: The Lagna holds a malefic with Gulika in a trine, or Gulika joins a kendra/trikona lord, or the lagna lord conjoins Rahu, Saturn or Ketu — a caution yoga classically linked to suspicion, fear of being cheated, swindled or robbed; clear boundaries and verifying people/deals directly help.", "Shakata Yoga: The Moon occupies the 6th, 8th or 12th house from Jupiter — a 'cart' yoga of fluctuating fortune, where hard-won gains and setbacks tend to alternate through life.", "Dehakashta Yoga: The lagna lord joins a malefic or sits in the 8th house — a Dehakashta yoga pointing to reduced bodily comfort.", "Krisanga Yoga (I): The lagna lord occupies a dry sign or one owned by a dry planet — a Krisanga yoga for a lean body and bodily aches.", "Jada Yoga: The 2nd lord in the 10th house joins malefics, or the 2nd is joined by the Sun and Mandi — becomes nervous in public assemblies.", "Grihanasa Yoga (I): The 4th lord in the 12th, aspected by a malefic — loses all house property.", "Kapata Yoga (I): The 4th house is joined by a malefic while the 4th lord is afflicted by malefics — a Kapata yoga for a hypocritical streak.", "Bhaga Chumbana Yoga: The 7th lord joins Venus in the 4th, or the lagna lord is debilitated — indulgence in sensual pleasures.", "Khalawata Yoga: The Ascendant falls in a malefic sign, aspected by malefics — early baldness.", "None of these are predictions of misfortune — they are areas where awareness and moderation protect your progress."]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 16, "total": 23, "id": "practical_recommendations", "title_en": "Practical recommendations", "title_ne": "व्यावहारिक सुझाव", "body": ["Play to your strengths — learning, good judgement and steady growth. This is where progress comes easiest for you.", "Don't avoid your weaker side — confidence and leadership. Build it up slowly with small, regular habits instead of waiting until you feel ready.", "Save big decisions for the good times highlighted above, so you act when the timing is on your side.", "Pick one small habit for each priority below and stick with it for the next three months."]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 17, "total": 23, "id": "spiritual_practices", "title_en": "Traditional spiritual practices (optional)", "title_ne": "पारम्परिक उपाय (वैकल्पिक)", "body": ["These are traditional, faith-based remedies offered as optional support — they are cultural practices, not requirements or guarantees.", "For strengthening Sun themes, classical texts suggest its weekday observance, charity associated with Sun, and respectful, calm conduct in that life area.", "Gratitude practices around Jupiter themes help you make the most of an existing strength.", "Above all, ethical action (sadachara) and steadiness are the remedies every tradition agrees on."], "optional": true}
{"kind": "section", "index": 18, "total": 23, "id": "planet_by_planet", "title_en": "Planet by planet", "title_ne": "ग्रह विश्लेषण", "body": [], "items": [{"label": "Sun (सूर्य)", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["D1: Sun in a friendly sign", "D9: vargottama (same sign in navamsa — reinforced)", "Shadbala: Borderline"], "text": "Sun is in Dhanu at 27°04′ (birth star Uttara Ashadha, quarter 1), in your 11th house; and is well supported there; in the same sign in both main charts (vargottama), which makes it noticeably stronger. In life it stands for soul, vitality, father, authority and self-confidence. Its overall strength is borderline."}, {"label": "Moon (चन्द्र)", "confidence": "tentative", "factors": [], "text": "Moon is in Mesha at 19°53′ (birth star Bharani, quarter 2), in your 3rd house; and is in a neutral spot there. In life it stands for mind, emotions, mother, comfort and the public. Its overall strength is adequate."}, {"label": "Mars (मंगल)", "confidence": "moderate", "factors": ["D1: Mars in a friendly sign", "D9: vargottama (same sign in navamsa — reinforced)"], "text": "Mars is in Dhanu at 27°16′ (birth star Uttara Ashadha, quarter 1), in your 11th house; and is well supported there; very close to the Sun (combust), so its outer results take extra effort; in the same sign in both main charts (vargottama), which makes it noticeably stronger. In life it stands for energy, courage, drive, siblings and property. Its overall strength is adequate."}, {"label": "Mercury (बुध)", "confidence": "moderate", "factors": ["D9: Mercury dignified in navamsa", "Shadbala: Strong"], "text": "Mercury is in Dhanu at 8°36′ (birth star Mula, quarter 3), in your 11th house; and is in a neutral spot there. In life it stands for intellect, communication, commerce and learning. Its overall strength is strong."}, {"label": "Jupiter (बृहस्पति)", "confidence": "strong", "factors": ["D1: Jupiter in a friendly sign", "D9: vargottama (same sign in navamsa — reinforced)", "Shadbala: Strong"], "text": "Jupiter is in Vrishchika at 14°30′ (birth star Anuradha, quarter 4), in your 10th house; and is well supported there; in the same sign in both main charts (vargottama), which makes it noticeably stronger. In life it stands for wisdom, ethics, wealth, teachers, children and grace. Its overall strength is strong."}, {"label": "Venus (शुक्र)", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["D1: Venus in a friendly sign", "Shadbala: Strong", "D9: Venus weak in navamsa"], "text": "Venus is in Makara at 28°18′ (birth star Dhanishta, quarter 2), in your 12th house; and is well supported there. In life it stands for love, partnership, beauty, comfort and the arts. Its overall strength is strong."}, {"label": "Saturn (शनि)", "confidence": "tentative", "factors": ["D9: Saturn weak in navamsa"], "text": "Saturn is in Dhanu at 1°16′ (birth star Mula, quarter 1), in your 11th house; and is in a neutral spot there. In life it stands for discipline, endurance, work, service and longevity. Its overall strength is adequate."}, {"label": "Rahu (राहु)", "confidence": "tentative", "factors": [], "text": "Rahu is in Vrishchika at 29°50′ (birth star Jyeshtha, quarter 4), in your 10th house. In life it stands for ambition, foreign and unconventional paths, obsession."}, {"label": "Ketu (केतु)", "confidence": "tentative", "factors": [], "text": "Ketu is in Vrishabha at 29°50′ (birth star Mrigashira, quarter 2), in your 4th house. In life it stands for detachment, intuition, past mastery and liberation."}]}
