{"kind": "section", "index": 21, "total": 23, "id": "yoga_explanations", "title_en": "Yogas in your chart", "title_ne": "योग", "body": ["A yoga is a specific planetary combination that inclines the chart toward a particular tendency. Below are the yogas formed in your chart, with the strength of the planets involved and whether the running dasha is activating them."], "items": [{"label": "Kala Sarpa Yoga", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "All seven tara grahas fall on one side of the Rahu–Ketu axis with none breaking out of the nodal hemisphere — a pattern associated with karmic intensity and sudden reversals in life direction.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Sunapha Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "Planets (other than the Sun) occupy the 2nd house from the Moon — a Chandra yoga for self-made prosperity and reputation built through personal effort.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Vanchana Chora Bheeti Yoga", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "The Lagna holds a malefic with Gulika in a trine, or Gulika joins a kendra/trikona lord, or the lagna lord conjoins Rahu, Saturn or Ketu — a caution yoga classically linked to suspicion, fear of being cheated, swindled or robbed; clear boundaries and verifying people/deals directly help.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Shakata Yoga", "confidence": "tentative", "polarity": "caution", "text": "The Moon occupies the 6th, 8th or 12th house from Jupiter — a 'cart' yoga of fluctuating fortune, where hard-won gains and setbacks tend to alternate through life.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Amala Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "A natural benefic occupies the 10th house from the Lagna or the Moon — a spotless (amala) reputation yoga for ethical conduct and lasting public respect.", "factors": []}, {"label": "Parvata Yoga", "confidence": "moderate", "polarity": "benefic", "text": "Benefics occupy angular houses while the 6th and 8th ho