{"kind": "section", "index": 6, "total": 25, "id": "finances", "title_en": "Finances & wealth", "title_ne": "धन / वित्त", "body": ["This area of life is about wealth, speech, family lineage and nourishment. The planet in charge of it, Venus, currently sits in the part of your chart about courage, and is in a neutral spot there (overall strength adequate). Planets currently in this area: Moon.", "This area of life is about gains, networks, aspirations and elder siblings. The planet in charge of it, Moon, currently sits in the part of your chart about wealth, and is in a neutral spot there (overall strength strong). Planets currently in this area: Rahu.", "Jupiter, the planet naturally linked to wealth and good fortune, is in Mesha (your 8th house) — well supported there.", "A wealth-forming Dhana yoga supports accumulation through steady earning and saving habits.", "Finances respond best to systematic saving; the chart describes tendencies, while habits decide outcomes."], "confidence": "strong", "factors": ["D1: natural benefic(s) present — Moon", "Shadbala: 11th lord Strong", "D1: malefic(s) in an upachaya house (strengthening here) — Rahu", "Yoga: Dhana yoga present"]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 7, "total": 25, "id": "relationships", "title_en": "Relationships & partnership", "title_ne": "सम्बन्ध", "body": ["This area of life is about partnership, marriage, business and public dealings. The planet in charge of it, Jupiter, currently sits in the part of your chart about transformation, and is well supported there (overall strength borderline).", "Venus, the planet linked to love and partnership, is in Vrishchika (your 3rd house) — in a neutral spot there. It describes what you value and look for in closeness.", "A challenging influence on the partnership house suggests relationships mature through some testing — open communication and shared values smooth the path. This is a tendency, not a fixed outcome."], "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["D1: 7th lord falls in the 8th (a difficult house)", "Shadbala: 7th lord Borderline"]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 8, "total": 25, "id": "family", "title_en": "Family & home", "title_ne": "परिवार", "body": ["This area of life is about home, mother, inner peace, property and education. The planet in charge of it, Jupiter, currently sits in the part of your chart about transformation, and is well supported there (overall strength borderline). Planets currently in this area: Sun, Mercury.", "This area of life is about fortune, dharma, higher learning, mentors and the father. The planet in charge of it, Venus, currently sits in the part of your chart about courage, and is in a neutral spot there (overall strength adequate).", "This area of life is about courage, effort, siblings, communication and skill. The planet in charge of it, Mars, currently sits in the part of your chart about work, and is in a neutral spot there (overall strength exceptional). Planets currently in this area: Venus.", "The 4th reflects mother and home, the 9th the father and elders, the 2nd the wider family, and the 3rd siblings."], "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["D1: natural benefic(s) present — Mercury", "D1: 4th lord falls in the 8th (a difficult house)", "Shadbala: 4th lord Borderline", "D1: natural malefic(s) present — Sun"]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 9, "total": 25, "id": "health_wellbeing", "title_en": "Health & wellbeing", "title_ne": "स्वास्थ्य", "body": ["In Vedic astrology, your vitality is read from the rising sign, its ruling planet, and the Moon; the 6th house describes illness, recovery and daily routine.", "Your rising-sign ruler Mercury (in your 4th house, in a neutral spot there) asks for proactive self-care — regular sleep, movement and stress management have outsized benefit.", "This area of life is about work, service, health, competition and obstacles. The planet in charge of it, Saturn, currently sits in the part of your chart about transformation, and is weak and needing conscious effort there (overall strength strong). Planets currently in this area: Mars.", "This is wellbeing guidance from chart tendencies, not medical advice; consult a qualified professional for any concern."], "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["D9: Mercury dignified in navamsa", "Shadbala: Borderline"]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 10, "total": 25, "id": "spiritual_growth", "title_en": "Spiritual growth", "title_ne": "आध्यात्मिक विकास", "body": ["This area of life is about fortune, dharma, higher learning, mentors and the father. The planet in charge of it, Venus, currently sits in the part of your chart about courage, and is in a neutral spot there (overall strength adequate).", "This area of life is about release, expenses, retreat, foreign lands and liberation. The planet in charge of it, Sun, currently sits in the part of your chart about home, and is well supported there (overall strength adequate).", "Jupiter in house 8 points to where wisdom, ethics and mentorship naturally develop.", "Ketu in house 5 (Makara) shows where you carry instinctive mastery and a pull toward detachment."], "confidence": "tentative", "factors": []}
{"kind": "section", "index": 11, "total": 25, "id": "current_life_phase", "title_en": "Current life phase", "title_ne": "वर्तमान जीवन-कालखण्ड", "body": ["You're in Saturn's main life period (mahadasha) until 12 Mar 2033, and the current sub-phase within it (antardasha) belongs to Mars, from 14 Sep 2026 to 24 Oct 2027. This phase emphasises discipline, hard work, responsibility, structure and patience.", "Saturn sits in your 8th house and rules your 5th, 6th houses, so the period concentrates on transformation and the houses it rules. It is weak and needing conscious effort — These results tend to arrive readily.", "Within it, the Mars sub-period sharpens the theme of drive (linked to your 6th house) until 24 Oct 2027."], "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["Shadbala: Strong", "Dasha: Saturn runs the current mahadasha", "D1: Saturn weak and needing conscious effort"]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 12, "total": 25, "id": "life_journey", "title_en": "Life journey — past, present & future", "title_ne": "जीवन यात्रा — विगत, वर्तमान र भविष्य", "body": ["Your life is divided into long chapters (called mahadashas in astrology), and each one emphasises a different part of life. Below are the chapters you have already lived, the one running now, and the ones ahead — with ages — so you can see at a glance which stage of life emphasises what."], "items": [{"label": "Jupiter life period (balance at birth) · age 0–14 (past)", "confidence": "mixed", "text": "1 Jan 2000 → 12 Mar 2014 (14 yrs): This chapter built experience around growth, wisdom, teaching, finances, children and good counsel."}, {"label": "Saturn life period · age 14–33 (present · you are here)", "confidence": "mixed", "text": "12 Mar 2014 → 12 Mar 2033 (19 yrs): You are living this chapter now — discipline, hard work, responsibility, structure and patience is foregrounded."}, {"label": "Mercury life period · age 33–50 (ahead)", "confidence": "mixed", "text": "12 Mar 2033 → 12 Mar 2050 (17 yrs): This coming chapter brings study, communication, trade, writing and analytical work to the fore."}, {"label": "Ketu life period · age 50–57 (ahead)", "confidence": "tentative", "text": "12 Mar 2050 → 12 Mar 2057 (7 yrs): This coming chapter brings detachment, specialisation, inner work and spiritual turns to the fore."}, {"label": "Venus life period · age 57–77 (ahead)", "confidence": "tentative", "text": "12 Mar 2057 → 11 Mar 2077 (20 yrs): This coming chapter brings relationships, comfort, creativity, the arts and material ease to the fore."}, {"label": "Sun life period · age 77–83 (ahead)", "confidence": "moderate", "text": "11 Mar 2077 → 12 Mar 2083 (6 yrs): This coming chapter brings leadership, recognition, dealings with authority and matters of the father to the fore."}, {"label": "Moon life period · age 83–93 (ahead)", "confidence": "tentative", "text": "12 Mar 2083 → 11 Mar 2093 (10 yrs): This coming chapter brings emotional life, home, public contact and care-giving to the fore."}, {"label": "Mars life period · age 93–100 (ahead)", "confidence": "strong", "text": "11 Mar 2093 → 12 Mar 2100 (7 yrs): This coming chapter brings drive, property, technical or competitive effort and bold initiative to the fore."}, {"label": "Rahu life period · age 100–118 (ahead)", "confidence": "tentative", "text": "12 Mar 2100 → 12 Mar 2118 (18 yrs): This coming chapter brings ambition, unconventional or foreign avenues and rapid change to the fore."}]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 13, "total": 25, "id": "dasha_timeline", "title_en": "Life-period timeline (with dates)", "title_ne": "जीवन-कालखण्ड तालिका", "body": ["The schedule of sub-periods inside your current Saturn life period, and the big life periods that follow — the most precise timing layer of your chart."], "items": [{"label": "Mars sub-period · running now", "confidence": "strong", "text": "14 Sep 2026 → 24 Oct 2027: drive — linked to your 6th house."}, {"label": "Rahu sub-period", "confidence": "tentative", "text": "24 Oct 2027 → 29 Aug 2030: ambition — linked to your 11th house."}, {"label": "Mercury life period (next major chapter)", "confidence": "moderate", "text": "Begins 12 Mar 2033, lasting to 12 Mar 2050 (17 yrs): a study chapter."}, {"label": "Ketu life period (next major chapter)", "confidence": "moderate", "text": "Begins 12 Mar 2050, lasting to 12 Mar 2057 (7 yrs): a detachment chapter."}, {"label": "Venus life period (next major chapter)", "confidence": "moderate", "text": "Begins 12 Mar 2057, lasting to 11 Mar 2077 (20 yrs): a relationships chapter."}]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 14, "total": 25, "id": "outlook_12_months", "title_en": "Outlook — next 12 months", "title_ne": "आगामी १२ महिना", "body": ["The year ahead is led by Mars's sub-period (through 24 Oct 2027), bringing drive, property, technical or competitive effort and bold initiative to the fore.", "It is well placed (in your 6th house), so initiatives in its areas are favoured — a good window to push forward.", "A shift to come: the Rahu sub-period opens 24 Oct 2027, bringing ambition to the foreground."], "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["Shadbala: Strong", "Dasha: Saturn runs the current mahadasha", "D1: Saturn weak and needing conscious effort"]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 15, "total": 25, "id": "pursue_and_when", "title_en": "What to pursue & when", "title_ne": "के कुरामा लाग्ने र कहिले", "body": ["This section shows what to focus on and the best time for each one. Every life area below comes with the period that most favours it — try to line up your bigger decisions with those good times."], "items": [{"label": "Your strongest area", "confidence": "strong", "text": "You are naturally good at energy, courage and taking action — effort pays off fastest here, so put most of your energy into it. Best time for this: a good period running now (14 Sep 2026 → 24 Oct 2027)."}, {"label": "Career & work", "confidence": "mixed", "text": "Make your bigger moves in career, status and public role. Best time for this: an upcoming good period (12 Mar 2033 → 12 Mar 2050)."}, {"label": "Wealth & gains", "confidence": "tentative", "text": "Expand income streams, networks and aspirations. Best time for this: an upcoming good period (12 Mar 2083 → 11 Mar 2093)."}, {"label": "Relationships & partnership", "confidence": "mixed", "text": "Advance marriage, partnership or public collaboration. Best time for this: an upcoming good period (29 Aug 2030 → 12 Mar 2033)."}, {"label": "Learning, dharma & mentors", "confidence": "tentative", "text": "Invest in higher learning, travel, mentors and spiritual practice. Best time for this: an upcoming good period (12 Mar 2057 → 11 Mar 2077)."}]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 16, "total": 25, "id": "opportunities", "title_en": "Opportunities", "title_ne": "अवसर", "body": ["The 11th house (gains) is well supported — a natural area to invest energy.", "Gaja-Kesari Yoga: Formed when Jupiter sits in an angle (kendra) from the Moon — a classic combination for good judgement, respect and steady fortune that tends to ripen with maturity.", "Sunapha Yoga: Planets (other than the Sun) occupy the 2nd house from the Moon — a Chandra yoga for self-made prosperity and reputation built through personal effort.", "Veshi Yoga: Planets occupy the 2nd house from the Sun — a Surya yoga for truthful speech, integrity and recognition through principled action.", "Vasi Yoga: Planets occupy the 12th house from the Sun — a Surya yoga for charity, spiritual merit and influence through selfless service.", "Ubhayachari Yoga: Planets flank the Sun on both the 2nd and 12th sides — a balanced Surya yoga for all-round ability, balanced temperament and success in both worldly and dharmic pursuits.", "Budha-Aditya Yoga: Formed when the Sun and Mercury share a sign, favouring intelligence, clear expression and analytical or administrative ability (strongest when Mercury is not too close/combust).", "Raja Yoga: Formed when the angular lord (Jupiter) and the trine lord (Saturn) join in one house — a Raja-yoga pattern supporting rise in status, provided the planets involved are reasonably strong.", "Harihara Brahma Yoga: Formed by any of three classical combinations linking the 2nd, 7th or Lagna lord with specific benefic placements — a Harihara Brahma yoga for eminent scholarship, truthfulness and a helpful nature.", "Ardha Chandra Yoga: All seven planets occupy seven contiguous houses beginning from a Panapara or Apoklima house — an Ardha Chandra yoga for fine features, lifelong happiness and command.", "Pasa Yoga: All seven planets spread across exactly 5 distinct sign(s) (a Sankhya Nabhasa yoga) — classically: Acquires wealth righteously, surrounded by friends and relatives.", "Sareera Soukhya Yoga: The lagna lord, Jupiter or Venus occupies an angle — a Sareera Soukhya yoga for long life, wealth and political favour.", "Sumukha Yoga (II): Benefics join the 2nd house — an attractive, smiling face.", "Bhratruvriddhi Yoga: The 3rd lord, Mars, or the 3rd house is joined or aspected by benefics — happiness through prosperous brothers.", "Bandhu Pujya Yoga (II): The 4th house or its lord has the association or aspect of Jupiter — respected and loved by relatives and friends.", "Nishkapata Yoga (I): The 4th house is occupied by a benefic, a dignified planet, or is itself a benefic sign — a Nishkapata yoga for a pure heart that hates secrecy and hypocrisy.", "Nishkapata Yoga (II): The lagna lord joins the 4th house with or aspected by a benefic — a Nishkapata yoga for a pure heart that hates secrecy and hypocrisy.", "Matru Sneha Yoga: The lagna and 4th lords share lordship, are natural or temporal friends, or the 4th is aspected by a benefic — cordial relations between mother and son.", "Vahana Yoga (I): The lagna lord joins the 4th, 9th, or 11th house — material comforts and conveyances.", "Satkalatra Yoga: The 7th lord or Venus links to Jupiter or Mercury — a noble, chaste and virtuous spouse.", "Raja Yoga (III): Two to four planets possess Digbala (directional strength) — a ruler even from an ordinary family."]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 17, "total": 25, "id": "cautions", "title_en": "Areas for caution", "title_ne": "सावधानी", "body": ["Keep a steady hand with transformation (the 8th house) — manage rather than force.", "Keep a steady hand with work (the 6th house) — manage rather than force.", "Dehakashta Yoga: The lagna lord joins a malefic or sits in the 8th house — a Dehakashta yoga pointing to reduced bodily comfort.", "Rogagrastha Yoga: The lagna lord in the ascendant joins a 6th/8th/12th lord, or a weak lagna lord sits in an angle or trine — a Rogagrastha yoga for a delicate constitution prone to sickness.", "Krisanga Yoga (I): The lagna lord occupies a dry sign or one owned by a dry planet — a Krisanga yoga for a lean body and bodily aches.", "Asatyavadi Yoga: The 2nd lord sits in a sign of Saturn or Mars while malefics occupy an angle and a trine — the native tends toward untruthfulness.", "Sraddhannabhuktha Yoga: Saturn owns or joins the 2nd lord, or the 2nd is aspected by a debilitated Saturn — food from death ceremonies.", "Bandhubhisthyaktha Yoga: The 4th lord is associated with malefics or sits in an inimical/debilitated sign — deserted by relatives.", "Matrunasa Yoga (I): The Moon is hemmed in between, joined by, or aspected by malefics — a very early death of the mother.", "Kapata Yoga (I): The 4th house is joined by a malefic while the 4th lord is afflicted by malefics — a Kapata yoga for a hypocritical streak.", "Matru Satrutwa Yoga: The lagna and 4th lords are natural or temporal enemies — ill feeling between mother and son.", "Aputra Yoga: The 5th lord sits in a dusthana — no issues at all.", "Vrana Yoga: A malefic 6th lord occupies the Lagna, 8th or 10th — tumours, boils or cancer.", "None of these are predictions of misfortune — they are areas where awareness and moderation protect your progress."]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 18, "total": 25, "id": "practical_recommendations", "title_en": "Practical recommendations", "title_ne": "व्यावहारिक सुझाव", "body": ["Play to your strengths — energy, courage and taking action. This is where progress comes easiest for you.", "Don't avoid your weaker side — clear thinking, communication and learning. Build it up slowly with small, regular habits instead of waiting until you feel ready.", "Save big decisions for the good times highlighted above, so you act when the timing is on your side.", "Pick one small habit for each priority below and stick with it for the next three months."]}
{"kind": "section", "index": 19, "total": 25, "id": "spiritual_practices", "title_en": "Traditional spiritual practices (optional)", "title_ne": "पारम्परिक उपाय (वैकल्पिक)", "body": ["These are traditional, faith-based remedies offered as optional support — they are cultural practices, not requirements or guarantees.", "For strengthening Mercury themes, classical texts suggest its weekday observance, charity associated with Mercury, and respectful, calm conduct in that life area.", "Gratitude practices around Mars themes help you make the most of an existing strength.", "Above all, ethical action (sadachara) and steadiness are the remedies every tradition agrees on."], "optional": true}
{"kind": "section", "index": 20, "total": 25, "id": "planet_by_planet", "title_en": "Planet by planet", "title_ne": "ग्रह विश्लेषण", "body": [], "items": [{"label": "Sun (सूर्य)", "confidence": "moderate", "factors": ["D1: Sun in a friendly sign", "D9: Sun dignified in navamsa"], "text": "Sun is in Dhanu at 16°32′ (birth star Purva Ashadha, quarter 1), in your 4th house; and is well supported there. In life it stands for soul, vitality, father, authority and self-confidence. Its overall strength is adequate."}, {"label": "Moon (चन्द्र)", "confidence": "tentative", "factors": ["Shadbala: Strong"], "text": "Moon is in Tula at 21°30′ (birth star Vishakha, quarter 1), in your 2nd house; and is in a neutral spot there. In life it stands for mind, emotions, mother, comfort and the public. Its overall strength is strong."}, {"label": "Mars (मंगल)", "confidence": "strong", "factors": ["D9: Mars dignified in navamsa", "Shadbala: Exceptional", "Dasha: Mars runs the current antardasha"], "text": "Mars is in Kumbha at 3°23′ (birth star Dhanishta, quarter 4), in your 6th house; and is in a neutral spot there. In life it stands for energy, courage, drive, siblings and property. Its overall strength is exceptional."}, {"label": "Mercury (बुध)", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["D9: Mercury dignified in navamsa", "Shadbala: Borderline"], "text": "Mercury is in Dhanu at 9°13′ (birth star Mula, quarter 3), in your 4th house; and is in a neutral spot there; very close to the Sun (combust), so its outer results take extra effort. In life it stands for intellect, communication, commerce and learning. Its overall strength is borderline."}, {"label": "Jupiter (बृहस्पति)", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["D1: Jupiter in a friendly sign", "Shadbala: Borderline"], "text": "Jupiter is in Mesha at 6°00′ (birth star Ashwini, quarter 2), in your 8th house; and is well supported there. In life it stands for wisdom, ethics, wealth, teachers, children and grace. Its overall strength is borderline."}, {"label": "Venus (शुक्र)", "confidence": "tentative", "factors": ["D9: Venus dignified in navamsa"], "text": "Venus is in Vrishchika at 10°23′ (birth star Anuradha, quarter 3), in your 3rd house; and is in a neutral spot there. In life it stands for love, partnership, beauty, comfort and the arts. Its overall strength is adequate."}, {"label": "Saturn (शनि)", "confidence": "mixed", "factors": ["Shadbala: Strong", "Dasha: Saturn runs the current mahadasha", "D1: Saturn weak and needing conscious effort"], "text": "Saturn is in Mesha at 9°06′ (birth star Ashwini, quarter 3), in your 8th house; and is weak and needing conscious effort there; moving backwards for now (retrograde), so its themes turn inward and get revisited. In life it stands for discipline, endurance, work, service and longevity. Its overall strength is strong."}, {"label": "Rahu (राहु)", "confidence": "tentative", "factors": [], "text": "Rahu is in Karka at 15°03′ (birth star Pushya, quarter 4), in your 11th house. In life it stands for ambition, foreign and unconventional paths, obsession."}, {"label": "Ketu (केतु)", "confidence": "tentative", "factors": [], "text": "Ketu is in Makara at 15°03′ (birth star Shravana, quarter 2), in your 5th house. In life it stands for detachment, intuition, past mastery and liberation."}]}
